    "euler": "edge once puzzle",
    "wrong_source": "Continue from the vertex where the red marker stands.",
    "already_used": "That edge is already orange; each edge may be used only once.",
    "hands_empty": "Put down what you hold before tracing the board.",
    "wrong_endpoint": "A completed trail must end at C.",
    "incomplete": "Use all seven edges before claiming the trail.",
    "already_claimed": "This completed trail has already been claimed.",
    "start": "Begin at A. Trace unused incident edges; orange edges cannot be retraced. The red marker shows the current vertex. One solution is A-B-D-C-A-D-E-C. These first four steps return to A. Reset clears this board only. Changes commit at hand contact; the marker jumps between labelled vertices, without physical bridge travel or an animated drawn stroke.",
    "finish": "After A-B-D-C-A, continue A-D-E-C and claim all seven used edges for green feedback. The trail A-C-D-E-C is a premature dead end: reset to try another route."
